1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,550
How much have U.S. Starbucks customers left unspent in the app?

2
00:00:04,570 --> 00:00:09,635
About $1.75 billion, over 2.3 trillion won

3
00:00:09,655 --> 00:00:13,440
When the balance runs low, the app tops up $25 automatically

4
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:20,319
2 trillion sits there, but 4 trillion flows in and out every three months

5
00:00:20,339 --> 00:00:24,641
On the books, it's a debt Starbucks repays in coffee

6
00:00:24,661 --> 00:00:29,588
No interest, no due date. I'd borrow on those terms too

7
00:00:29,608 --> 00:00:34,644
So does Starbucks earn big interest on it?

8
00:00:34,664 --> 00:00:40,204
Smaller than you'd think. For every 100 won Starbucks kept from coffee in FY2025

9
00:00:40,224 --> 00:00:44,111
Interest plus other income on its cash: just 4 won

10
00:00:44,131 --> 00:00:52,759
Breakage, money nobody ever spends, is close to 8 won, twice the interest

11
00:00:52,779 --> 00:00:56,164
So the real power of stored value isn't interest

12
00:00:56,184 --> 00:01:00,692
With $12 left in the app, the coffee next door feels like a waste

13
00:01:00,712 --> 00:01:08,857
35.8M Rewards members make up 59% of U.S. company-store sales. Stored value made regulars

14
00:01:08,877 --> 00:01:12,556
A money tip: load only a month's worth

15
00:01:12,576 --> 00:01:17,922
Money left in the app may be picking your next coffee for you

16
00:01:17,942 --> 00:01:24,244
Like and subscribe for more. Full video: profile link
